          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em (weakly) stable Yang-Mills-Higgs pair
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %em (weakly) stable YMH connection
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills-Higgs+pair"} Yang-Mills-Higgs pair
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            is positive or even strictly positively curved.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills-Higgs+pairs"} Yang-Mills-Higgs pairs
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/critical+points"} critical points
            of the Yang-Mills-Higgs action functional, where the first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational
            derivative vanishes. For (weakly) stable Yang-Mills connections, the second derivative is additionally required to be positive or even strictly positive.
